# No spaghetti — decomposition law

## File size (hard)

| Lines | Action |
|-------|--------|
| >600 | **Must split** before next feature ship |
| >1000 | **P0 debt** — split before any P1 polish |
| >1500 | **Ship blocker** for unrelated features |

Current P0 fat files: `quest_tracker_map.lua`, `quest_tracker_gather.lua`, `quest_tracker_window.lua`, `quest_data_loader.lua`.

## Split pattern (REFramework)

- `local M = package.loaded["name"] or {}; package.loaded["name"] = M` reload guard
- `function M.install(ctx)` — unpack ctx once, return API table
- One concern per file: child stack, row draw, frame loop, map pins, gather NPC scan
- **No** new 50-line branches inside `M.install` — extract helper module first

## Forbidden

- Symptom hacks in an already-busy draw path
- Second copy of the same ImGui begin/end logic
- Full `_qt_refresh_row_caches` on tab click (refilter only)
- `message.get` during load_gui / post_save / AV streak

## Ship gate

- `_ship_check.ps1` must pass
- Grok TAKE/ADAPT on any new ImGui or hook pattern
- Line count noted in SHIP HANDOFF if touching a >600 file without splitting
